     2	
     3	Speaks the `ql-udf` wire protocol over stdio: reads frames from **stdin**, replies
     4	on **stdout**. stdout is the PROTOCOL channel — the worker must NEVER print to it;
     5	diagnostics go to stderr. The engine (`ql-udf::ProcessWorker`) spawns this, performs
     6	the HELLO/HELLO_ACK handshake, and sends one CALL per UDF invocation.
     7	
     8	UDFs are registered by handle via `quantbook.register_formula_function`. The trusted
     9	user module that does the registering is named by the ``QUANTBOOK_UDF_MODULE`` env
    10	var and imported once at startup (its import side-effects populate the registry).
    11	"""
