    17	/// Outcome of a failed UDF dispatch. Every variant maps to a *deterministic*
    18	/// engine-side result at the call site (6.4-3c) — a cell error value + a
    19	/// `CellDiagnostic` — never a panic and never a silently-dropped failure
    20	/// (No-Fallbacks; contract §10.4 exit tests 6 + 7).
    21	///
    22	/// **6.4-3b completed the taxonomy** (the M3 item the 6.4-3a audit filed): the
    23	/// process-backed [`crate::process::ProcessWorker`] can hit `Handshake` (the
    24	/// `HELLO`/`HELLO_ACK` protocol-version exchange failed) and `Protocol` (a
    25	/// malformed control frame), and `Cancelled` is reserved for a cooperative/hard
    26	/// cancel distinct from a deadline `Timeout` (exit test 6 treats user-cancel and
    27	/// deadline-breach differently; the v1 hard-cancel mechanism is worker-kill →
    28	/// `Timeout`, with `Cancelled` wired when cooperative `CANCEL` lands).
    29	#[derive(Debug, thiserror::Error)]
    30	pub enum UdfError {
    31	    /// The Python callable raised. Maps to `#CALC!`/`#VALUE!` + a diagnostic
    32	    /// carrying `exc_type` + `message` (exit test 7).
    33	    #[error("udf raised {exc_type}: {message}")]
    34	    Raised { exc_type: String, message: String },
    35	    /// The call exceeded its deadline. The worker is killed; the result (if any
    36	    /// arrives late) is dropped (exit test 6). Maps to `#TIMEOUT!`.
    37	    #[error("udf timed out after {0:?}")]
    38	    Timeout(Duration),
    39	    /// The call was cancelled (cooperative `CANCEL` / hard cancel) BEFORE a
    40	    /// deadline breach — distinct from [`UdfError::Timeout`] so the engine can
    41	    /// surface a cancel diagnostic rather than `#TIMEOUT!` (exit test 6).
    42	    #[error("udf call cancelled")]
    43	    Cancelled,
    44	    /// The worker handshake failed: the worker reported an incompatible protocol
    45	    /// version. Maps to `#CALC!` + a diagnostic; the worker is not usable.
    46	    #[error("udf worker handshake: protocol mismatch (engine {expected}, worker {got})")]
    47	    Handshake { expected: u32, got: u32 },
    48	    /// The worker spoke a malformed/unexpected frame (a wire-protocol violation
    49	    /// that is neither a clean `Raised` nor a codec error). Maps to `#CALC!`.
    50	    #[error("udf worker protocol violation: {0}")]
    51	    Protocol(String),
    52	    /// The worker process died / the transport broke. Maps to `#CALC!` + a
    53	    /// diagnostic; the worker respawns lazily on the next call.
    54	    #[error("udf worker died / transport broken: {0}")]
    55	    WorkerDied(String),
    56	    /// Args could not be encoded, or the result could not be decoded.
    57	    #[error("udf codec: {0}")]
    58	    Codec(#[from] CodecError),
    59	}
    60	
    61	/// Dispatch one UDF call: marshal `args`, invoke the worker function identified by
    62	/// `handle`, and return its result grid — subject to `deadline`.
    63	///
    64	/// Implementations must guarantee: a `deadline` breach surfaces
