     1	//! `ql-udf` — out-of-process Python UDF worker transport + codec.
     2	//!
     3	//! **Phase 6.4-3 (the wedge).** Design: `docs/phase6/6-4-3-design.md`. This crate
     4	//! owns the *mechanics* of talking to a managed Python worker process: the wire
     5	//! protocol (length-prefixed frames), the Arrow ↔ engine-`Value` codec, and the
     6	//! [`UdfWorker`] abstraction. It is a **leaf** (dependency-inversion, mirroring
     7	//! `ql-io-csv` / `ql-io-xlsx`): it depends only on `ql-types`, `arrow`, and
     8	//! `thiserror`, and is consumed by `ql-exec` at the dispatch site (6.4-3c), which
     9	//! adapts `FunctionArg`/`FunctionReturn` ↔ [`ql_types::ArrayValue`] and injects a
    10	//! worker into the eval context.
    11	//!
    12	//! **Modules:**
    13	//! - [`codec`] — `ArrayValue` ⇄ Arrow IPC stream bytes (the "fiddly part"). The
    14	//!   decoder is a trust boundary for worker-controlled bytes: it validates the exact
    15	//!   schema and rejects null/non-finite/short-column/reordered/trailing-batch input
    16	//!   loudly, never panicking (6.4-3a + its audit-fix).
    17	//! - [`frame`] — the `[u32 LE len][u8 type][payload]` envelope + [`frame::FrameType`].
    18	//! - [`payload`] — the typed `CALL` / `RETURN` data payloads ([`payload::CallPayload`]
    19	//!   `{ handle, call_id, args }` / [`payload::ReturnPayload`] `{ call_id, result }`).
    20	//! - [`control`] — the `HELLO` / `HELLO_ACK` / `RAISE` / `LOG` / `CANCEL` control-frame
    21	//!   payload codecs + [`control::PROTOCOL_VERSION`] (6.4-3b pinned these; 6.4-3a left
    22	//!   them opaque).
    23	//! - [`worker`] — the [`worker::UdfWorker`] trait + the [`worker::UdfError`] taxonomy
    24	//!   + an in-process [`worker::MockWorker`] (test double).
    25	//! - [`process`] — [`process::ProcessWorker`]: the real, process-backed worker
    26	//!   (6.4-3b) that spawns `python -m quantbook.worker`, handshakes, calls, and
    27	//!   timeout-kills/respawns. Implements [`UdfWorker`].
    28	//!
    29	//! It is a **leaf** (dependency-inversion, mirroring `ql-io-csv` / `ql-io-xlsx`):
    30	//! depends only on `ql-types`, `arrow`, `thiserror`, and `std`. `ql-exec` will consume
    31	//! it at the dispatch site (6.4-3c), adapting `FunctionArg`/`FunctionReturn` ↔
    32	//! [`ql_types::ArrayValue`] and injecting a worker into the eval context.
    33	//!
    34	//! **Deferred** to later 6.4-3 cycles: the eval-site `RegisteredFn::Udf` dispatch arm
    35	//! (6.4-3c); debugpy attach + trusted-workspace gating + IDE handle-minting +
    36	//! `LOG`→`CellDiagnostic` routing (6.4-3d). The on-wire batch format is Arrow IPC
    37	//! (so the Python side uses `pyarrow` natively); the [`codec`] boundary keeps it
    38	//! swappable. The Python worker lives in `crates/quantbook-py/python/quantbook/`.
    39	
    40	pub mod codec;
    41	pub mod control;
    42	pub mod frame;
    43	pub mod payload;
    44	pub mod process;
    45	pub mod worker;
    46	
    47	pub use frame::{Frame, FrameType};
    48	pub use payload::{CallPayload, ReturnPayload};
    49	pub use process::{ProcessWorker, PythonWorkerConfig};
    50	pub use worker::{MockWorker, UdfError, UdfWorker};

